    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1358": {
      "title": "LAB INSTRUCTOR, PHYSICS",
      "description": "LAB INSTRUCTOR, PHYSICS  | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In LAB INSTRUCTOR, PHYSICS Req #212 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, June 18, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Tuesday, September 15, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY All required documents must be uploaded to Additional Documents with correct titles for each required document. The Department of Mathematics, Physics & Geology in the School of Science & Technology at CBU invites applications for a full-time Lab Instructor, Physics at the rank of Lab Instructor . This position will commence in January 2027. One of Canada’s youngest and most ambitious universities, CBU recognizes its location on Cape Breton Island as part of Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq people. CBU offers a comprehensive set of liberal arts, science, and professional programs and a unique commitment to community, economic development, aboriginal learning, and research into many aspects of environment and culture. CBU delivers an authentic multicultural experience to all who become part of its academic community. Surrounded by pristine natural landscape, vibrant culture, and welcoming communities on Canada’s stunning east coast, CBU attracts students from more than 50 countries around the world. Our faculty bring passion to their teaching and research and we are known for our friendly and inclusive culture. Strong community involvement and a spirit of entrepreneurship enhance CBU's position in post-secondary education. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching labs in support of our Physics courses and be responsible for maintenance and management of Physics lab equipment .  There is potential to teach labs associated to Calculus and Statistics as well as the occasional delivery of Physics courses at the introductory level. The minimal qualification required is a bachelor's degree in physics with teaching experience at the post-secondary level .  However, the department of Mathematics, Physics, and Geology gives strong preference to candidates with a Masters degree in an area of experimental physics and direct experience in maintenance/management of experimental equipment. Applications for the successful candidate will include an: Cover Letter Current CV Teaching Statement Document describing relevant experience in reference to the descriptions above (If the candidate received their degree after 2023, university transcripts are required) List of at least three references. Short listed candidates will be required to submit two reference letters. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications may not be considered. CBU teaches programs on campus, off campus in locations across and outside of Canada, and on-line. The university and its partners will therefore provide opportunities for faculty members to teach in different modes in different locations as part of their regular workload. While these opportunities may not be available equally for all faculty positions in all programs, a clear willingness to teach in different modes and locations will be noted as part of your application. The union affiliation of this position is with the Cape Breton University Faculty Association. Applications must be received by September 15 th , 2026 . Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResources@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family CBUFA Faculty Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow us to share information with third party advertising and analytics partners and use your information for advertising and analytics purposes. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL": {
      "title": "Search Jobs",
      "description": "Job Board | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Search Jobs Search by job title, keywords, req ID Location Distance Advanced search Clear All Search Jobs Sessional Instructors in Mi'kmaq Studies Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Posted Tuesday, September 1, 2026 | Expires Friday, November 6, 2026 Cape Breton University’s Mi’kmaq Studies and Unama’ki College are seeking applicants interested in teaching specific courses in the fall or winter term on campus, online, or in community. We are seeking qualified L’nu sessional instructors who may be available to teach courses that become available over the next two years. We anticipate ongoing teaching needs in areas such as:\n\nMi’kmaw Language classes\nMi’kmaw History classes\nMi’kmaw Traditional Governance \nOther areas of Mi’kmaw knowledge and expertise\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity for individuals who are interested in exploring a future teaching career, while sharing their knowledge and experience with students. If you are thinking of possible future at CBU, this is a great way to see if teaching is for you!\nThe ideal candidates will possess:\n\nA graduate degree in a relevant discipline; and/or applicants who do not hold a Master's degree but have significant traditional, cultural, community-based, or professional knowledge will also be considered for courses that align with their area of expertise.\n\n\nExperience teaching in First Nations communities;\n\n\nRelevant qualifications, experience, or demonstrated expertise in the subject area being taught.\n\n \nTEACHING ON CAMPUS: MI’KMAQ STUDIES\nSituated within the School of Arts and Social Science (SASS), Mi’kmaq Studies advances Mi’kmaw knowledge and scholarship in support of students developing academic critical thinking skills and awareness of Mi’kmaw perspectives and knowledges. Mi’kmaq Studies fosters engaged citizens who can interact respectfully with Mi’kmaw communities, contribute to self-determination, and understand the importance of upholding treaty and rights-based responsibilities. It is available as a major, double major, and concentration in the Bachelor of Arts (BA) and as a major or double major in the Bachelor of Arts Community Studies (BACS). \nWe are seeking instructors who can teach in this area on campus, and sometimes online. Fall and winter courses typically run for 12 weeks.\nTEACHING OFF-CAMPUS: IN-COMMUNITY PROGRAMMING\nFor more than 30 years, Unama’ki College’s In-Community Degree Programs have been making post-secondary education more accessible to Indigenous students by offering tailored degree programming across Mi’kma’ki. Students have the opportunity to earn a degree from CBU while studying at home, close to their families and supports systems in addition to receiving specialized student support from CBU. \nWe seek instructors who are interested in teaching courses in-community, which are taught in a more condensed timeline (4 to 8 weeks).\nApplications for the successful candidate will include a:\n \n\ncover letter describing the expertise of the applicant\ncomplete resume\nlist of at least three references. \n\n \nPlease upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications may not be considered.\nApplications will be accepted on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed as teaching opportunities arise.\nTo learn more about these opportunities, prospective applicants are invited to attend one of two online information sessions. Details, including dates and times, will be posted on the Unama’ki College Facebook page. Read More Req# 222 Research Manager - Project Homeward Bound Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Posted Tuesday, August 25, 2026 | Expires Friday, September 25, 2026 Cape Breton University (CBU) is accepting applications for a Research Manager to join a transformative, multi-year research initiative titled Homeward Bound: Enhancing Healthcare, Housing, and Social Support for Aging Rural Nova Scotians. Funded by Research Nova Scotia, this 7-year initiative aims to support aging in the right place (AIRP) by improving the integration of healthcare, housing, and social supports in rural communities across Nova Scotia’s Eastern Health Zone. \nThis ambitious project brings together a multidisciplinary team spanning social work, architecture, nursing, medicine, computer science, economics, and policy, in partnership with communities, government, and academic institutions. Find out more here: www.homewardboundns.ca \nAbout the Role\nThis position will be responsible for managing financial and other research operations of the Homeward Bound project, working closely with the Project Manager, Research Coordinator, and Research Leads. \nThe successful candidate will play a central leadership role in ensuring compliance with the project protocols and objectives and applying specialized knowledge to budget management, reporting, and forecasting. Depending on qualifications, the candidate may also support creation and compliance of the project’s data management plan and ethics applications/clearances across multiple institutions. \nThis is a full-time, remote and/or hybrid position reporting to the Co-Principal Investigator overseeing Research & Finance (Dr. Kelsey Harvey) and working within a multidisciplinary team. The appointment is for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding and project needs.\nKey Responsibilities \nFinancial Operations and Oversight \n• Coordinate financial activities related to the grant. \n• Develop budgets for the research project(s). \n• Forecast lifespan of budget, identifying possible gaps and opportunities. • Process expense claims. \n• Monitor health of the budget. \n• Support developing estimates of time, human, and financial resources needed to support the research plan. \n• Document deviations from budget and communicate these to funder. \n• Work closely with finance office to reconcile budgets. \n• Prepare budget reports for internal and external partners. \n• Maintain confidentiality. \nDepending on qualifications, additional responsibilities may include: \nData Management & Governance \n• Assist with the creation and implementation of the project’s data management plan. \n• Laise with appropriate parties to communicate the data management plan. \n• Update the data management plan as needed. \n• Audit for compliance with the data management plan. \n• Coordinate data sharing agreements across institutions as applicable. \n• Maintain systems for de-identification, consent tracking, and secure storage. \nEthics \n• Support the preparation and submission of research ethics applications and amendments across multiple institutions, both academic and in healthcare. \n• Track ethics applications across multiple institutions. \n• Keep records related to reporting needs to ethics offices. \n• Maintain confidentiality. \nResearch Operations & Administrative Leadership \n• Support coordination of interdisciplinary research activities across project teams, facilitating research meetings and check-ins as needed. \n• Ensure research staff have the operational supports and tools required to carry out research activities effectively. \n• Support reporting, documentation, and project tracking in collaboration with the Project Manager and Research Leads.\n \nRequired Qualifications: \n• Undergraduate degree in a relevant discipline. \n• Minimum of 2 years’ experience managing a research project budget of over $1 million annually. \n• Demonstrated ability to manage a large-scale budget. \n• Demonstrated experience supporting team development, management, or workforce coordination. \n• Proficiency in Microsoft Office, including SharePoint and Microsoft Teams. \n• Excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage competing priorities in a large interdisciplinary research team. \n \nPreferred Qualifications: \n• Master’s or PhD in a relevant discipline. \n• Experience managing multi-million dollar and multi-year interdisciplinary research projects. \n• Demonstrated commitment to anti-oppressive, community-engaged, and equity-informed practices. \n• Experience with qualitative and/or quantitative research methods and interdisciplinary research. \n• Experience and knowledge related to data management or a willingness to learn. \n• Experience with multi-institutional research ethics applications. \n• Experience with community-based and/or clinical research. \n \nApplications for the successful candidate will include a: \n• Complete resume / CV. \n• Cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant. \n• List of at least three references. \n \nPlease upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications may not be considered.\n \nSalary Range: $80,000 – $90,000 annually\n \nApplications must be received by 11:00PM on September 25, 2026. Read More Req# 189 Mailroom/Print Shop Clerk Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Posted Thursday, August 20, 2026 | Expires Friday, September 4, 2026 Cape Breton University invites applications for a Mailroom / Print Shop Clerk to join our team in this full-time continuing position.\n \nAs an essential part of the University’s day-to-day operations, the successful candidate will help keep information, materials, and services moving efficiently across campus. This position is responsible for coordinating incoming and outgoing mail, packages, and courier deliveries; supporting University shipping and receiving activities; and providing day-to-day operational support to the University’s Print Shop.\n \nKey Responsibilities:\n \nMailroom & Receiving\n\nCoordinate incoming and outgoing mail, packages, and courier services.\nSort and distribute mail and deliveries across the University.\nPrepare shipments, estimate postage, and operate postage equipment.\nTrack missing or time-sensitive shipments and liaise with couriers as needed.\nManage university mailboxes and keys.\nReceive, record, and distribute incoming goods and materials.\nPrepare receiving and month-end billing reports.\n\n \nPrint Shop Support\n\nOperate photocopiers, printers, computers, and related equipment.\nPrioritize and complete print jobs efficiently and within deadlines.\nProvide cost estimates for internal and external clients.\nProduce and finish a variety of documents, including course materials, exams, forms, and correspondence.\nBind, laminate, and prepare documents as required.\nReport equipment issues and provide Print Shop coverage when needed.\n\n \nPhysical Demands:\nRequires walking, standing, bending, and lifting (boxes, mail bags, etc).\n \nQualifications:\n\nCompletion of High School Diploma\n1 year of related experience is considered an asset\nDemonstrated proficiency in the use of computerized systems and databases (MS Office and Email) with the ability to learn updated and/or new software quickly required\nAbility to work quickly and accurately with attention to detail\nDemonstrated interpersonal and communication skills, including good customer service\n\n \nApplications for the successful candidate will include a:\n\ncover letter describing the expertise of the applicant\ncomplete resume\nlist of at least three references. \n\nPlease upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications may not be considered.\n \nThe union affiliation of this position is with the Canadian Union of Public Employees (CUPE) Local 3131. Salary level is Band A2. Read More Req# 220 CBMC, Simulation Project Manager Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Posted Wednesday, August 5, 2026 | Expires Sunday, September 13, 2026 CBU invites applications for the full-time continuing position of Simulation Project Manager to support the launch and ongoing operations of the simulation-based education program within the Cape Breton Medical Campus.\n \nThe Simulation Project Manager will lead the design, development, implementation, and delivery of simulation training that supports both undergraduate and postgraduate medical education in Cape Breton. This role will be integral to curriculum support, faculty development, and clinical education across CBMC’s teaching sites.\n \nReporting to the Assistant Deans of Pre-Clerkship and Clerkship, the incumbent will develop a comprehensive implementation plan, coordinate faculty training, and ensure technical and pedagogical excellence in simulation programming.\n \nKey Responsibilities\n \nProgram Development:\n\nDesign and implement simulation lab procedures and policies.\nDevelop high-quality simulation scenarios aligned with medical education accreditation standards.\nSupport the integration of simulation into undergraduate and postgraduate medical curricula.\nTrain faculty in simulation pedagogy, including pre-briefing, facilitation, and debriefing.\nEstablish a framework for evaluating learner outcomes and simulation effectiveness.\nPrepare operational and staffing budgets for simulation-related activities.\n\n \nProgram Delivery & Operations:\n\nCoordinate simulation-based events and clinical education sessions.\nDevelop schedules for simulation activities aligned with curriculum timelines.\nSupport faculty in simulation instruction at both CBMC and affiliated clinical sites.\nFoster a respectful and safe learning environment grounded in reflection and confidentiality.\n\n \nTechnical Oversight & Administration:\n\nMaintain an inventory of simulation equipment across CBMC and clinical teaching sites.\nEstablish systems for equipment maintenance, cleaning, repairs, and usage tracking.\nProvide on-site technical support and troubleshooting.\nEnsure alignment with current simulation safety protocols and best practices.\n\n \nQualifications and Skills\n\nFormal education with a focus on adult education or health profession degree.  Certification as a Healthcare Simulation Educator will be considered an asset;  \nA minimum of five years progressive experience in the health/medical education field including project management and educational programming;  \n\n\nClinical knowledge and experience in health care related fields such as EMT, paramedical or other health professional certification and training;\nCertification and experience in course delivery for BLS, ACLS, PALS and NRP would be considered an asset;  \nDemonstrated analytical and problem-solving skills;\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to present technical and non-technical audiences;\nExperience managing multiple major clients either internally or in a professional services environment;\nHighly efficient team player, with the ability to also work independently in a fast-paced, fluid environment;\nMechanical and technical skills to competently maintain and use equipment in the simulation’s Centre’s;\nOrganizational and time management skills to keep materials in order, track various projects, maintain files and follow through assignments to completion;\nPhysical ability to lift, move, maintain and set up computer, audio-visual and simulation lab equipment weighing up to 50 lbs. without assistance.\n\n \nWorking Conditions\n\nSome evening and weekend work required to support simulation events. Must have access to reliable transportation. \nTravel to clinical sites across Nova Scotia will be expected.\n\n \nApplications for the successful candidate will include a:\n\ncover letter describing the expertise of the applicant\ncomplete resume\nlist of at least three references. \n\nPlease upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications may not be considered.\n \nApplications must be received by 11:00pm on September 13th, 2026. Read More Req# 219 LAB INSTRUCTOR, PHYSICS Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Posted Thursday, June 18, 2026 | Expires Tuesday, September 15, 2026 The Department of Mathematics, Physics & Geology in the School of Science & Technology at CBU invites applications for a full-time Lab Instructor, Physics at the rank of Lab Instructor. This position will commence in January 2027.\n \nOne of Canada’s youngest and most ambitious universities, CBU recognizes its location on Cape Breton Island as part of Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq people. CBU offers a comprehensive set of liberal arts, science, and professional programs and a unique commitment to community, economic development, aboriginal learning, and research into many aspects of environment and culture. \n \nCBU delivers an authentic multicultural experience to all who become part of its academic community. Surrounded by pristine natural landscape, vibrant culture, and welcoming communities on Canada’s stunning east coast, CBU attracts students from more than 50 countries around the world. Our faculty bring passion to their teaching and research and we are known for our friendly and inclusive culture. Strong community involvement and a spirit of entrepreneurship enhance CBU's position in post-secondary education. \n \nThe successful candidate will be responsible for teaching labs in support of our Physics courses and be responsible for maintenance and management of Physics lab equipment.  There is potential to teach labs associated to Calculus and Statistics as well as the occasional delivery of Physics courses at the introductory level.\n \nThe minimal qualification required is a bachelor's degree in physics with teaching experience at the post-secondary level.  However, the department of Mathematics, Physics, and Geology gives strong preference to candidates with a Masters degree in an area of experimental physics and direct experience in maintenance/management of experimental equipment.\n \nApplications for the successful candidate will include an:\n \n\nCover Letter\nCurrent CV\nTeaching Statement\nDocument describing relevant experience in reference to the descriptions above(If the candidate received their degree after 2023, university transcripts are required)\nList of at least three references. Short listed candidates will be required to submit two reference letters.\n\n \nPlease upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications may not be considered.\n \nCBU teaches programs on campus, off campus in locations across and outside of Canada, and on-line. The university and its partners will therefore provide opportunities for faculty members to teach in different modes in different locations as part of their regular workload. While these opportunities may not be available equally for all faculty positions in all programs, a clear willingness to teach in different modes and locations will be noted as part of your application.\n \nThe union affiliation of this position is with the Cape Breton University Faculty Association.\n \nApplications must be received by September 15th, 2026. Read More Req# 212 1 ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow us to share information with third party advertising and analytics partners and use your information for advertising and analytics purposes. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
