    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1496": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Special Projects",
      "description": "Coordinator, Special Projects | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Coordinator, Special Projects Req #225 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, September 24, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, October 9, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Cape Breton University (CBU) is seeking an organized, collaborative, and highly motivated professional to join its Athletics Department as a Full-Time Limited-Term Coordinator, Special Projects . This approximately 18-month position plays a key role in supporting the planning, coordination, and delivery of special projects, events, and initiatives within the Athletics Department. As a key member of the department, the Special Projects Coordinator will serve as a primary point of contact and work closely with internal and external stakeholders to coordinate activities, provide administrative support, and oversee day-to-day project and event requirements. SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Plan and coordinate Athletics special events, student-athlete recognition programs, tournaments, fundraising initiatives, camps, and game-day experiences. Build relationships and engagement with University departments, community partners, student groups, and external organizations to support Athletics events, promotions, and initiatives. Support departmental operations and priorities including risk management, the Student-Athlete Advisory Committee (SAAC), marketing initiatives, and the planning and execution of special projects. Provide administrative and operational support to the Department of Athletics & Recreation, including communications, scheduling, document preparation, records management, office operations, and confidential student information. Coordinate Athletics logistics and travel , including team transportation and accommodations, itineraries, travel documentation, scheduling changes, and related administrative requirements. QUALIFICATIONS: Post-Secondary diploma in a recognized field . Undergraduate degree is an asset; Candidates with an undergraduate degree combined with appropriate experience will be considered ; Exceptional oral and written communications ; friendly, helpful, professional. Strong time management skills and ability to perform multiple tasks simultaneously and meet deadlines; Knowledge and interest in university sport and community recreation development; Understanding of all aspects of risk management with respect to health and safety. Excellent computer, internet, and information technology skills , including proficiency in Microsoft Office, and the ability to learn new technology tools quickly. Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant complete resume list of at least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications may not be considered. Applications must be received by 11:00PM on October 9th, 2025 . Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family NON_UNION Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1485": {
      "title": "Knowledge Mobilization and Community Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "Knowledge Mobilization and Community Engagement Specialist | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Knowledge Mobilization and Community Engagement Specialist Req #223 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Sunday, September 20, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Sunday, October 11, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Cape Breton University (CBU) is accepting applications for a Knowledge Mobilization and Community Engagement Specialist to join a transformative, multi-year research initiative titled Homeward Bound: Enhancing Healthcare, Housing, and Social Support for Aging Rural Nova Scotians . Funded by Research Nova Scotia, this 7-year initiative aims to support aging in the right place (AIRP) by improving the integration of healthcare, housing, and social services in rural communities across Nova Scotia’s Eastern Health Zone. This ambitious project brings together a multidisciplinary team spanning social work, architecture, nursing, medicine, pharmacy, computer science, economics, and policy, in partnership with communities, government, and academic institutions. Find out more here: www.homewardboundns.ca PURPOSE: The Knowledge Mobilization and Community Engagement Specialist supports the Communication bucket of the Homeward Bound NS project, working under the supervision of Dr. Sheryl Bourgaize (Co-PI, Communications) and collaborating closely with Dr. Alison Grittner (Co-PI Community). The position is responsible for leading the development and execution of knowledge mobilization strategies, coordinating communications across internal and external channels, and supporting the translation of research findings for community, sector, and public audiences. This is a full-time hybrid role based in Cape Breton, NS . The appointment is for one year, with renewal depending on funding and project needs . Salary Range: $68,000–$78,000 CAD annually SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and implement a strategic knowledge mobilization and communications plan aligned with the goals, values, and EDI commitments of Homeward Bound NS; Develop and implement community-engagement strategies in project communities that align with research activities; Create key messages and communications materials to support the project’s media relations and public engagement; Advise the Communications Co-PI on best practices for knowledge mobilization, storytelling, and community-engaged communication; Track and report on engagement metrics, adjusting knowledge mobilization and communications strategies based on feedback and performance data; Work in alignment with Homeward Bound communications and branding guidelines (including language the project avoids, such as “patients,” “stakeholders,” and ageist terminology); Create and manage content for multiple platforms including the project website, social media, newsletters, press releases, blog posts, and multimedia materials (e.g., videos, infographics); Translate research findings and project activities into accessible language for diverse communities and public audiences; Coordinate production of print and digital knowledge mobilization products including community reports, research summaries, and multimedia materials; Supervise a student worker responsible for managing the project’s social media platforms and website content; Prepare briefing materials, progress reports, and communications updates for the Governance Collective and project partners; Build and maintain relationships with external partners, community groups, and sector partners; Liaise with communications teams at partner organizations and post-secondary institutions; Identify and engage new community and sector audiences with the project’s key messages, activities, and research findings; Plan, promote, and coordinate project-related conferences, workshops, community events, and knowledge mobilization activities; Manage event communications including promotion, registration, and post-event reporting; Support co-design workshops and community engagement events in coordination with the research team; Coordinate internal project communications including team newsletters, meeting materials, and shared online platforms; Establish guidelines and protocols for effective communication within the project team; Prepare information notes, memos, and briefing materials on behalf of the Co-PI team; Support the development and implementation of the project’s Authorship and Intellectual Property policy in collaboration with the Communications Co-PI; Assist with knowledge dissemination activities consistent with project IP guidelines and open-access commitments; Uphold EDI, Reconciliation, and Feminist Governance values in all work, reflecting the project’s commitment to Etuaptmumk (Two-Eyed Seeing) and anti-oppressive practice. QUALIFICATIONS and SKILLS: Bachelor’s degree in communications, Public Relations, Knowledge Mobilization, Public Health, Social Sciences, or a related field, OR an equivalent combination of professional experience and community-based communication work. Master’s degree is an asset ; Minimum 2–3 years of professional experience in knowledge mobilization, research communications, or a related field Demonstrated experience developing and executing integrated communications strategies for multiple platforms and audiences Exceptional written and verbal communication skills , including experience writing for diverse audiences across multiple formats (social media, newsletters, press releases, reports) Strong organizational and project management skills; ability to prioritize multiple tasks and work independently in a fast-paced environment Understanding of and commitment to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) principles, including Etuaptmumk (Two-Eyed Seeing) and anti-oppressive communication practice Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience working in research, academic, or community-based organization Familiarity with design tools (e.g., Canva, Adobe Creative Suite) and website management platforms (e.g., WordPress) Experience with social media management and digital analytics tools Anti-racist training, as is experience working with Indigenous communities Experience supervising student workers or research assistants Applications for the successful candidate will include a: Cover letter describing the expertise and interest of the applicant Complete resume Writing sample (knowledge mobilization, research communications, or public relations preferred) List of at least three references Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications may not be considered. Applications must be received by 11:00PM on October 11, 2026 Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family NON_UNION Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1481": {
      "title": "Rink Attendant",
      "description": "Rink Attendant | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Rink Attendant Req #224 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, September 17, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, October 2, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Cape Breton University invites applications for a full-time continuing position as Rink Attendant . We are seeking a candidate who is available to commence employment as soon as possible and join our team in supporting the day-to-day operations and maintenance of the rink facility. The successful candidate, during ice plant operation is responsible for ice maintenance, building and equipment maintenance (including preventive maintenance) in the Arena.  When the ice plant is not in service, the arena will function as an off-ice facility, during those times the successful candidate will also participate in maintenance and event facilitation in the arena complex, other recreational facilities, or around the campus; and operate a variety of equipment in the performance of duties. Shift work: The Rink Attendant will have shift work, including weekends and holidays, in response to event demands.  Working hours are scheduled by the Arena Manager. Working conditions and physical effort: Work involves exposure to chemicals and corrosive materials and the operation of equipment.  Incumbent may be exposed to temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke and/or loud noises. The incumbent must follow all safety precautions and use personal protective equipment. Work may involve the use of a variety of equipment. Considerable physical activity including heavy lifting, pulling, pushing, walking, etc. Physical work is a primary part of this position. Qualifications of this role are: High school diploma or GED. Valid Power Engineering Class 4 ticket or Refrigeration Class 2. Minimum of one (1) year related experience. Current First Aid course, AED and CPR, or willingness to obtain and re-certify as required. Demonstrated initiative to carry out job responsibilities with general direction including good judgment skills. Physically fit in order to be able to carry out the requirements of the position. Ability to wear a respirator. Demonstrated good work safety record. Knowledge of regulatory procedures, and provincial Codes/Standards. Thorough knowledge of area plant operations and safety protocols. Knowledge of occupational hazards and safety precautions, the N.S. OHS Act , WHMIS. Applications for the successful candidate will include: A cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant A complete CV including a list of publications Proof of Valid Power Engineering Class 4 ticket or Refrigeration Class 2. A list of least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications may not be considered. The union affiliation of this position is with the Nova Scotia Government and General Employees Union. Local 19, Maintenance Classification (MOS). Applications must be received by 11:00PM on October 2, 2026 Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family NSGEU MOS Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1461": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Psychology (Limited Term)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Psychology (Limited Term) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Assistant Professor, Psychology (Limited Term) Req #217 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, September 3, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Monday, October 5, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY All required documents must be uploaded to Additional Documents with correct titles for each required document. The Department of Psychology in the School of Science and Technology at Cape Breton University (CBU) invites applications for a Full-Time Limited Term position in Psychology at the rank of Assistant Professor ( or Lecturer depending on qualifications ) in an open area of specialization . We welcome applications from all areas of psychology and are particularly interested in candidates with strong expertise in research methodology and quantitative analysis. This position will commence January 1, 2027 to December 24, 2027 (or as soon as possible thereafter). The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate courses that fit departmental needs, including Introduction to Psychology, Data Analysis, and Research Methods. The ability to teach courses in the areas of research methods and data analysis is a requirement. The ability to teach in additional areas including advanced statistics, psychometrics, and courses in the candidate’s own area of specialization would provide additional assets to fit our needs. The candidate will also be expected to supervise undergraduate honors thesis students and participate in program development. CBU delivers an authentic multicultural experience to all who become part of its academic community. Surrounded by pristine natural landscape, vibrant culture, and welcoming communities on Canada’s stunning east coast, CBU attracts students from more than 50 countries around the world . Our faculty bring passion to their teaching and research and we are known for our friendly and inclusive culture. Strong community involvement and a spirit of entrepreneurship enhance CBU's position in post-secondary education. The Department of Psychology has 9 full-time members with 8 tenured or tenure-track faculty members whose research spans several fields and who strongly commit to undergraduate teaching and research. Faculty members may have opportunities to teach in various formats and locations as part of their regular workload. While not all faculty positions will have the same opportunities , applicants can express their willingness to teach in diverse modes and settings. The successful candidate is expected to develop a strong research program and should demonstrate their research background and will support their research plans. The capacity to seek funding for their research program and supervise undergraduate student research assistants in their research program is also expected. Applicants must demonstrate their research can be successful in the CBU context. Applicants are expected to demonstrate potential and commitment with regard to teaching, research/creative/scholarly activities, and service to Cape Breton University, community and profession. The successful candidate is expected to undertake appropriate service activities within the university community. Candidates should have a relevant PhD in psychology, with demonstrated strength in research methodology and quantitative analysis . In exceptional cases, candidates who are in the very late stages of their PhD may be considered with the successful completion of the PhD being a condition of employment. Also, Candidates with a relevant Master’s degree who have completed all of the requirements for a relevant PhD but are currently completing their dissertation may be considered for the rank of Lecturer. Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant statement of teaching philosophy evidence of effective teaching statement of research accomplishments and research program plans statement of how they incorporate equity, diversity and inclusiveness in their work and services complete CV including a list of publications list of at least three references. Short-listed candidates will be required to submit three reference letters. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications may not be considered. The union affiliation of this position is with the Cape Breton University Faculty Association. Applications must be received by October 5th, 2026 Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResources@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family CBUFA Faculty Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1391": {
      "title": "Regional Manager of In.Business",
      "description": "Regional Manager of In.Business | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Regional Manager of In.Business Req #210 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada This job posting is no longer available Job Description Posted Wednesday, July 8, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expired Friday, August 28, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Cape Breton University (CBU) is seeking a Regional Manager of In.Business for Unama’ki College . This is a full-time, limited-term position for approximately one year, with the possibility of renewal. The successful candidate will collaborate with the Director, Business Operations, to focus on high school student recruitment and encourage the study of business and related disciplines through the delivery of the established In.Business mentorship program. Worksite will include CBU’s Membertou Office. The successful candidate will: •    Executing strategic objectives and initiatives, including: o    identifying and recruiting Indigenous high school students. o    identifying and recruiting of Indigenous business mentors. o    establishing and maintaining key contacts; and o    identifying funding and other opportunities that benefit Unama’ki College. •    Establishing and maintaining productive partner, community, and stakeholder relationships, including collaboration with internal CBU schools and departments. •    Plan, coordinate, host a maximum of two conferences per year. •    Developing and maintaining a regional budget. •    Track project activities, timelines, deliverables, and outcomes to support successful program execution. •    Coordinate logistics related to meetings, events, travel, program activities, and operational requirements. •    Prepare and maintain reports, updates, and program documentation for internal and external stakeholders. •    Provide administrative and operational support, including scheduling, correspondence, and document management. •    Assist and support team members with ongoing initiatives, collaborative projects, and day-to-day operations. Other duties as assigned by the direct supervisor. The ideal candidate will require: • A Master’s Degree is preferred , but candidates with a Bachelor’s degree with extensive, demonstrated experience may be considered . Discipline areas of Business, Regional, and Community Economic Development and/or Education are preferred; •    Knowledge of Indigenous communities and experience working with and in communities is essential; •    Demonstrated capacity for proposal writing, administrative support, and reporting are essential; •    Demonstrated capacity for organization with attention to detail in a multi-task environment is required; •    A self-starter with a strong work ethic and able to work well with other disciplines is essential; •    Effective relationship management, strong verbal and written communication, and presentation skills are required; •    A demonstrated ability to deliver major collaborative partnerships with external partners in a timely and professional manner, including execution of multiple short- and long-term projects simultaneously; •    Proficiency with word processing, Excel spreadsheets, and PowerPoint presentation development; •    Willingness and ability to travel; •    Mi’kmaq language is considered a valued asset. Applications for the successful candidate will include a: •    cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant •    complete resume •    list of at least three references. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed. Incomplete applications may not be considered. Applications must be received by 11:00PM on August 28 , 2026 Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Job Details Job Family NON_UNION Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    }
